pus 5.5 had the lead at -8.8. F2 then lost 9.0 points, against the engine's E2, and brought the lead back to +0.2. The swings in this stretch were large on both sides."}, {"turn": 34, "text": "D3 decided the game. It lost 34.5 points, taking Black's lead from -1.9 to +32.6, while the engine preferred B2. Opus 5.5 never got back into the game after it."}, {"turn": 40, "text": "B3 lost another 11.8 points, with the engine preferring H8. Black's lead, already +30.8, grew to +42.6. The remaining moves changed little, and Opus 5.5 resigned at +44.2 for Black."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py flood-fills each group on a pasted board and prints its stones, liberties and a DANGER flag, and count.py counts stones and enclosed territory with named dead stones removed; b.txt is just a saved board. All of it only analyzes the current position, with no candidate moves scored, no playouts and no look-ahead.", "stop": false}}